# Describe your book's accessibility

A book can say how accessible it is: for example, that every picture has a description and the text can be read aloud. Online stores and reading apps show this to readers who need it before they buy or open the book.

These fields are in Advanced Mode.

1. Click [Settings]{.ui}, then [General]{.ui}, and tick [Advanced mode]{.ui}. Close the settings.
2. Click the [Book]{.ui} tab, then [Details]{.ui}.
3. Click [Advanced details]{.ui}.
4. Under [Accessibility]{.ui}, fill in the fields that describe your book. Start with the *Summary*, a sentence or two in plain words, then choose the *Accessibility features* the book has and any *Hazards*, such as flashing images.

Describe the book as it is, not as you mean it to be. Check it first, as described in Find accessibility problems.
